"# Provisional model specification\n\nThis specification reflects the **middle-ground responses from the group's\nendline survey**: for each question, the median answer of the group.\n\nPlease keep in mind:\n\n- This specification represents a **majority-supported scenario, not a final or\n  binding decision**.\n- The purpose is to understand **your individual reaction**, including any\n  reservations and objections.\n- **All positions, including disagreement, are legitimate and important.**\n- Your assessment is anonymous.\n\n\"An improvement\" means correctly identifying more students who are experiencing\nacademic difficulties out of 100 such students, while the number of students\nincorrectly flagged stays about the same.\n\n## Data the model may use\n\nThe model starts from course credits earned. Each further data type is added\nonly under this condition:\n\n| Data added | Condition |\n|---|---|\n| Course performance (grades, passed/failed and registered courses) | only if it identifies at least about 5 more students per 100 |\n| Admissions and enrolment data (high-school GPA, programme, school) | only if it identifies at least about 5 more students per 100 |\n| Absalon online course activity (page views, late submissions) | only if it identifies at least about 10 more students per 100 |\n\n## Sensitive data\n\n| Data type | If it improves identification | If it only improves fairness |\n|---|---|---|\n| Age | never acceptable | never acceptable |\n| Gender | never acceptable | only if it improves fairness across student groups |\n| Nationality | only if it identifies at least about 1-3 more students per 100 | never acceptable |\n| Disability-related information | never acceptable | never acceptable |\n| Race/ethnicity | never acceptable | never acceptable |\n| First-generation college student status | never acceptable | never acceptable |\n| Financial aid status | never acceptable | never acceptable |\n\n## Explainability\n\nThe starting point is a single clear rule (very high explainability). A less\nexplainable model is used only under this condition, compared to the next more\nexplainable level:\n\n| Explainability level | Condition |\n|---|---|\n| High (few clearly defined factors) | only if it identifies at least about 5 more students per 100 |\n| Moderate (many additive factors) | only if it identifies at least about 1-3 more students per 100 |\n| Low (limited, case-specific explanations) | never acceptable |\n| Very low (no meaningful case-specific explanation) | only if it identifies at least about 1-3 more students per 100 |\n\n## Fairness\n\n- To make the model work equally well across student groups, the group accepts:\n  about 1-3 fewer students identified per 100.\n- What should be equal across student groups: both goals equally."